            instructions_en: "Adjust the Smith machine seat height so the bar is at shoulder level. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and your knees slightly bent. Grip the barbell overhand, with your hands slightly wider than shoulder-width apart. Unrack the barbell and step back into a stable stance. Position the bar behind your head, resting it across your upper traps. Keep your core braced and your chest lifted throughout the exercise. Press the bar overhead until your arms are fully extended. Pause briefly at the top, then slowly lower the bar to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.",
