            instructions_en: "Set the Smith machine bar at shoulder height. Stand facing the bar with your feet shoulder-width apart. Grasp the barbell with an overhand grip, slightly wider than shoulder-width apart. Step back and position the bar across the fronts of your shoulders, resting it on your collarbones and deltoids. Keep your chest up, back straight, and core braced. Bend your knees and hips to lower your body as though sitting in a chair. Continue lowering until your thighs are parallel to the floor or slightly below. Pause briefly, then push through your heels to return to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.",
